** μέμφομαι**,
{{Refs 6th c.BC+|6th c.BC: Theognis Elegiacus 797, etc.}}: _imperfect_ ἐμέμφετο {{Refs|Batrachomyomachia 70}}: _future_ μέμψομαι {{Refs 8th c.BC+|8th-7th c.BC: Hesiodus Epicus “Opera et Dies” 186, etc.}}: _aorist_ ἐμέμφθην {{Refs 6th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 1.77, 3.13, 5th c.BC: Pindarus Lyricus “N.” 11.30 (κατα-), 5th c.BC: Euripides Tragicus “Hippolytus” 1402, +others, 5th c.BC: Thucydides Historicus 4.85 (in _passive_ sense, 1st c.AD: Philo Judaeus 1.301, 2nd c.AD: Apollonius Dyscolus Grammaticus “de Syntaxi;” 67.22): but in _Attic dialect_ and Trag. commonly ἐμεμψάμην, as 4th-5th c.BC: Aeschylus Tragicus “Prometheus Vinctus” 1073 (_anapaest meter_), 5th-6th c.BC: Andocides Orator 4.3, 5th c.BC: Thucydides Historicus 1.143, also in 6th c.BC: Mimnermus Lyricus 14.5, 5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 2.24}}: _present_ in _passive_ sense, {{Refs 2nd c.AD+|3rd c.AD(?): Diogenes Laertius 6.47, 2nd c.AD: Aspasius Philosophus “in Ethica Nicomachea commentaria - pars” 133.14:}}_future_ μεμφθήσομαι Ps.-{{Refs 4th c.BC+|4th-3rd c.BC: Menander Comicus in Meineke “Fragm.Comedy texts Gr.” iv p.337}}:—**blame, censure**, first in {{Refs 8th c.BC+|8th-7th c.BC: Hesiodus Epicus (though ἐπιμέμφομαι occurs in 8th c.BC: Homerus Epicus):}}
**1** with _accusative_ _person_, μέμψονται δ᾽ ἄρα τούς {{Refs 8th c.BC+|8th-7th c.BC: Hesiodus Epicus “Opera et Dies” 186, compare 6th c.BC: Theognis Elegiacus 797, 5th c.BC: Pindarus Lyricus “N.” 7.64, 5th c.BC: Sophocles Tragicus “Electra” 384, etc.; μ. τύχην 4th-5th c.BC: Aeschylus Tragicus “Prometheus Vinctus” 1073 (_anapaest meter_); μ. τὸν θέντα τὸν νόμον 5th-6th c.BC: Andocides Orator 4.3}}; κατὰ τὸ μαντήϊον οὐκ ὀρθῶς ὁ Κροῖσος μέμφεται (i.e. τὸν Λοξίαν) {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 1.91; μ. τινὰ πρὸς τοὺς φίλους 5th-6th c.BC: Xenophon Historicus “Oeconomicus” 11.23; μ. τινὰ εἴς τι [prev. author] “An.” 2.6.30.}}
**1.b** c._accusative_ _of things_, οἶνε, τὰ μέν σ᾽ αἰνῶ, τὰ δὲ μέμφομαι {{Refs 6th c.BC+|6th c.BC: Theognis Elegiacus 873}}; μ. τὴν γνώμην, τὰ δῶρα, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 1.207, 3.13; μ. τὴν φιλοσοφίαν 5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Euthydemus” 305b; ἄλλο οὐδὲν μ. 5th-6th c.BC: Xenophon Historicus “Anabasis” 7.6.39; μεμφθεὶς κατὰ τὸ πλῆθος τὸ ἑωυτοῦ στράτευμα 5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 1.77; ταῦτα.. προτ᾽ ἐμὸν θυμὸν ἐμεμψάμαν 3rd c.BC: Theocritus Poeta Bucolicus 30.24.}}
**2** with _dative_ _person_ et _accusative_ _of things_, **impute as blameworthy, cast in one's teeth**, {{Refs 7th c.BC+|7th-6th c.BC: Sappho Lyrica “Papyrus fragments” in E. Diehl, 14.7 (probably), 5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 3.4, 4.180, 5th-6th c.BC: Aristophanes Comicus “Nubes” 525, “Av.” 137, 5th c.BC: Thucydides Historicus 1.143, etc.: also with _accusative_ _cognate_, τῷ Λοξίᾳ μέμψιν μ. 5th-6th c.BC: Aristophanes Comicus “Plutus” 10, etc.}}; μ. τινὶ ὅτι.. {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 9.6, compare 6.92}}; οὕνεκα.. {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Euripides Tragicus “Helena” 31}}; εἰ.. {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Thucydides Historicus 4.85: with _dative_ _person_ et _genitive_ _of things_, οὔποτ᾽ ἀνδρὶ τῷδε κηρυκευμάτων μέμψει 4th-5th c.BC: Aeschylus Tragicus “Septem contra Thebas” 652:}} with _genitive_ _person_ et _accusative_ _of things_, ὃ μάλιστα μέμφονται ἡμῶν which is the chief **complaint they make** against us, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Thucydides Historicus 1.84.}}
**3** with _dative_ _person_ only, **to be dissatisfied with, find fault with**, {{NT+5th c.BC+|4th-5th c.BC: Aeschylus Tragicus “Septem contra Thebas” 560, “Pr.” 63, 5th c.BC: Sophocles Tragicus “Trachiniae” 470, 5th c.BC: Euripides Tragicus “Orestes” 285, “IA” 899 (troch.), 5th-6th c.BC: Xenophon Historicus “Memorabilia” 3.5.20, NT.Heb.8.8}}: with _participle_ added, μ. ἡμῖν λογισαμένοις {{Refs 5th c.BC+|2nd c.AD: Lucianus Sophista “Charid.” 20; ὡς κακῶς βουλευομένοις 5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Phaedrus” 234b, compare “Cri.” 50d.}}
**4** with _genitive_ _of things_ only, **complain of**, οὐ μάχης.. μέμψει {{Refs 5th c.BC+|4th-5th c.BC: Aeschylus Tragicus “Fragmenta - American Journal of Philology” 199.3; εἴ τι μέμφῃ τῆς ἐμῆς ἀπουσίας 5th c.BC: Euripides Tragicus “Hecuba” 962}}; τιμῆς ἐμέμφθη of her [neglected] honour {{Refs 8th c.BC+|compare (εὐχωλῆς ἐπιμέμφεται 8th c.BC: Ilias Homerus Epicus “Illiad” 1.93), 5th c.BC: Euripides Tragicus “Hippolytus” 1402; μ. τῶν γεγενημένων 5th c.BC: Thucydides Historicus 8.109.}}
**5** with _infinitive_ with μή, μ. μὴ πολλάκις βουλεύεσθαι **object** that one ought not.., {{Refs|[prev. author] 3.42.}}
**6** _absolutely_, **find fault, complain**, {{Refs 4th c.BC+|4th-5th c.BC: Aeschylus Tragicus “Supplices” 137 (Lyric poetry); ὅτι 4th c.BC: Aristoteles Philosophus “Ethica Nicomachea” 1162b18. in Law, οἱ μεμφόμενοι}} the **plaintiffs**, {{Refs|“GDI” 4998 (from Gortyn).}}
